// ArrayBlockingQueue: Fixed capacity, single lock
BlockingQueue<String> arrayQueue = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(1000);

// LinkedBlockingQueue: Optional capacity, dual-lock throughput
BlockingQueue<String> linkedQueue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(1000);

// Performance Tip: Always prefer LinkedBlockingQueue for high-concurrency 
// producer-consumer scenarios where throughput is the primary bottleneck.
